The Open-Source Analysis Lab (OSAL) collects primary and expert open sources that offer distinctive insight into a country — reporting by people inside the country (in any language), independent investigative outlets, in-country think tanks, pollsters, and subject-matter experts. Every source is scored on seven criteria so an analyst can judge quickly what a source is worth. See the Methodology for the scoring rubric and inclusion criteria.


